# Georgian Text in AutoCAD MCP

All user-facing text in drawings must be in **Georgian** unless the user
explicitly asks otherwise.

## Hard rules

1. **Never send Georgian via PowerShell**.
   PowerShell on Windows downgrades non-ASCII to `?`. Use a Node.js script
   (`axios.post(...)`) so the request body is real UTF-8.

2. **Always set the Georgian text style first**, once per drawing:
   ```
   (command "_.-STYLE" "GEO" "Sylfaen.ttf" "0" "1" "0" "N" "N" "N")
   ```

3. **Always wrap MText with the inline font override** so it renders even
   if a different style is current:
   ```js
   const ge = (text) => `\\FSylfaen|b0|i0;${text}`;
   await MText(x, y, ge('ფუნდამენტის გეგმა'), 600, 25000, 'TEXT');
   ```

4. For multi-line MText, separate lines with `\\P`, not `\n`.

5. Fallback fonts if Sylfaen is missing on the machine, in this order:
 `BPG Excelsior Caps`, `Arial Unicode MS`, `Noto Sans Georgian`.

## Office-existing styles (UNI / legacy DWGs)

When adapting an **existing** UNI / office DWG, do not force Sylfaen —
match the file's existing styles. Measured on UNI A2-A4, B1-B4 (see
`memory/uni-reference-extract-FACTS.md`):

| Style | Use |
|---|---|
| `geo` | Georgian body text — the office's day-to-day style |
| `geo-kolxetmtavruli` | Uppercase (Kolkheti Mtavruli) — titles |
| `chveumtavruli` / `ChveuMtavr` | Common Mtavruli — section titles |
| `Avaza Mtavruli` | Decorative Mtavruli — appears as inline override |
| `Arch-Dim` | dimension text |

For **new** drawings the AI generates from scratch, use Sylfaen as
above. For **edits to an existing UNI file**, set the current style to
`geo` or `geo-kolxetmtavruli` first and write text with that style.

